====================================================================================================
Part E. The A2 energy matrices are the TP-4 packet matrices M_(q,w)
====================================================================================================
E1. sympy, generic potential: M_(q,w) - (A2 matrix) = 0 for
    (B1) M = (2c + 1) I + sym DU + A: True
    (B4) M_1 = I - sym DU + A: True
    (B5) M_2 = (1 + c + V.D log omega) I - 2 sym DV + A: True
    (B6) M_3 = (1 + c + V.D log omega) I - 3 sym DV + A: True
    P95 M = (2c + 1) I + [[-2 chi22 - chi04, chi31], [chi31, chi22]]: True
    P95 M_1 = [1 - t(c + e)/5] I + [[-chi04, chi13], [chi13, -chi22]] (W2, k = 1): True
    P95 M_2 = [1 - c + (16/5) t(c + e)/(1 + 3t)] I + [[chi22 - chi04, (3 chi13 - chi31)/2], [., -2 chi22]]: True
    i.e. (B1) is q = -1 unweighted (the Hdot^-1 low energy), (B4) q = 1 unweighted, (W2) k = 1 is q = 1 with omega_1, (B5) = (W2) k = 2 is q = 2 with omega, (B6) is q = 3 with omega
